   338	**S61 — DROPS the three time comparisons.** Pilot: “Six blocks confirm it.” C5: “the three-conjunct predicate holds at k = 6.” The pilot supplies only the count, without even stating the inclusive counting convention. A9 510 preserves A2.1's predicate. A2.2, lines 222–224, gives:
   339	
   340	> `declared_issue_time − ε ≤ anchor_time`
   341	>
   342	> `anchor_time ≤ declared_issue_time + δ`
   343	>
   344	> `confirmed_at ≤ declared_issue_time + δ`
   345	
   346	A9 223 fixes ε = 24 h and δ = 72 h; A2.1 80–85 counts the anchor block as confirmation one and identifies the sixth block. Six confirmations alone do not establish those time comparisons.
