   360	The first bullet is the count condition; the remaining three are the three time comparisons. Keep these separate from the two issuance-window comparisons. These are Bitcoin time values, not a promise of real-time latency.
   361	
   362	### F18
   363	
   364	**S64 — ADDS an assurance of closeness to real time.** Pilot: “A Bitcoin block time is close to the real time, but it is not exact.” C5: “Header times are chain-time proxies.” A9 444–446: “Translating this into a finite UTC cutoff requires an additional, explicit backward-skew assumption that V1 does not establish: A2.1 registers no finite bound on B − C”. The pilot turns a proxy with an explicit unbounded backward residual into a closeness promise.
