   377	**S68 — CHANGES block-height coverage into an ambiguous time comparison and DROPS the all-header rule.** Pilot: “If T is after the last Bitcoin block in the trust file, the verdict is CANNOT VERIFY.” C6: “A selected anchor (C5) beyond the newest pin is `UNVERIFIABLE`. Every supplied header must be pinned.” T is a header time, not a block number; C5 itself says header times are not monotone. The selected anchor can be within the covered range while another supplied header is outside it.
