   340	6. Build `A_sig` and stamp its SHA-256. One stamp per receipt.
   341	7. Obtain and validate the confirmation and time evidence.
   342	8. Ship the complete receipt.
   343	
   344	[ENC §5.4:515-525; A9:278-281] That is eight steps in both sources. A retry that changes any committed byte needs a
   345	fresh stamp. The frame-only anchor is withdrawn, with no fallback. [A9:277; ENC §5.1:407-414]
   346	
   347	Issuer duties that are not verifier rules: an attempt whose T would exceed not-after is not shipped [A9:341-342]; the
   348	`gpg` signer refuses a frame whose `declared_issue_time` is more than ε from its clock [A9:327-330]; the issuer never
   349	re-authorizes a key [A9:260]; public publication of the commit stays an issuer duty [A9:413-418]; the issuer
   350	re-captures the DNSSEC snapshot before shipping if it fails the snapshot rule [DD:94].
   351	
   352	Further issuer duties [OWNER 2026-10-14]:
   353	- **Chain-order pre-commitment.** Do not issue in a window until the key-assertion commit's stamp has k = 6
   354	  confirmations and the receipt will anchor at a higher height (A9 C4). Before honest issuance the issuer obtains and
   355	  validates the git assertion's k = 6 proof. A receipt stamped after the issuer has observed h_git + 5 anchors above
   356	  it, so it passes the verifier's `h_git + 5 < h_receipt` rule (section 6.3). [G02; RB §5]
   357	- **Snapshot c3.** Check all three conjuncts on the snapshot's own proof before shipping; recapture or retry if they
   358	  fail. A snapshot stamped before the receipt need not confirm before it. [G06]
   359	- **DNSSEC support.** Validate the snapshot under this profile's algorithm set (section 6.1); do not ship a receipt
   360	  whose chain would be `DNSSEC_ALGORITHM_UNSUPPORTED`. [G16]
   361	- **Snapshot body.** Convert to the section 15.3 body before stamping. [G19]
   362	- **Signature output.** Both OpenPGP adapters emit signatures that satisfy the rule-O policy of section 8 before
   363	  signing is final and before stamping. [G11]
   364	- **Canonical container.** Emit the container as canonical JCS (section 15.1). [G17]
   365	- **Pre-ship checks for the 2026-10-14 r2 completions** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F07, r2-F08, r2-F09, r2-F10]: the
   366	  snapshot body carries no RRSIG with fewer Labels than its owner (section 15.3); the selected path of each of the
   367	  three proofs (receipt, snapshot, git) satisfies the transaction-shape subset and the conventional merkle suffix
   368	  (section 15.2), else the proof is re-stamped or the attempt abandoned; both OpenPGP adapters and the repository
   369	  signer emit type-16/type-33 subpackets only in the shapes section 8 allows. All 352 Bitcoin paths in the
   370	  repository's 129 proofs satisfy the shape and suffix rules (owner check, 2026-10-14); this is evidence, not a rule.
